WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.720
Welcome to Chemical Bonding.

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:06.460
This recorded Chemistry class uses an AI generated Marin voice.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:11.360
Bond formation can lower energy through interactions between nuclei and

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:11.820
electrons.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:16.540
The octet rule is a useful pattern, not the physical cause of every bond.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:21.840
Electron deficient species, odd electron species and expanded valence shell

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.360
descriptions show its limits.

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:28.740
An ionic solid is an extended lattice, not a collection of isolated pairs held

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:30.580
only by the act of electron transfer.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:35.940
For comparable structures, greater ionic charges and smaller separations

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:37.940
strengthen electrostatic attraction.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:43.100
In a Born Haber cycle, add all enthalpy steps with their stated signs.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:48.289
Lattice formation from gaseous ions releases energy, while separating the

00:00:48.289 --> 00:00:48.560
solid

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:52.780
into gaseous ions requires energy; tables may use either convention.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:56.540
Fajans's rules describe polarization and covalent character.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:01.500
A small, highly charged cation more strongly distorts a neighbouring electron

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:01.760
cloud.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:06.080
A large, readily polarizable anion is more easily distorted.

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:11.361
Thus lithium iodide has greater covalent character than lithium fluoride in

00:01:11.361 --> 00:01:11.520
the

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:12.240
usual comparison.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:17.380
The model describes trends, not a sharp boundary dividing every bond into

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:19.380
purely ionic or purely covalent.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:24.220
A quantitative lattice enthalpy calculation also needs consistent phases,

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:27.520
stoichiometric amounts and all the necessary energy data.

00:01:27.816 --> 00:01:31.576
Start a Lewis structure by counting valence electrons from all atoms.

00:01:32.496 --> 00:01:35.796
Add electrons for negative charge and subtract for positive charge.

00:01:36.516 --> 00:01:40.256
Draw a plausible connected skeleton, fill terminal shells where appropriate,

00:01:40.756 --> 00:01:43.476
then place remaining electrons and inspect the central atom.

00:01:44.476 --> 00:01:46.756
Carbon dioxide has sixteen valence electrons.

00:01:47.536 --> 00:01:51.696
Two carbon oxygen double bonds use eight electrons, and two lone pairs on each

00:01:51.696 --> 00:01:52.836
oxygen use the other eight.

00:01:53.116 --> 00:01:56.436
Each double bond still counts as one electron domain for shape.

00:01:56.436 --> 00:01:59.596
Hydrogen requires a duet, not an octet.

00:02:00.336 --> 00:02:04.676
Formal charge equals valence electrons minus nonbonding electrons minus half

00:02:04.676 --> 00:02:05.676
the bonding electrons.

00:02:06.416 --> 00:02:10.096
In ammonium, nitrogen has four single bonds and no lone pair.

00:02:10.816 --> 00:02:13.856
Five minus zero minus four gives formal charge plus one.

00:02:14.516 --> 00:02:18.556
Each hydrogen has formal charge zero, so the total is plus one as required.

00:02:19.416 --> 00:02:22.449
Formal charge differs from oxidation number and from an experimentally

00:02:22.449 --> 00:02:22.796
inferred

00:02:22.796 --> 00:02:23.476
partial charge.

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:28.076
In one carbonate contributor, the double bonded oxygen has formal charge zero

00:02:28.536 --> 00:02:32.636
and the two singly bonded oxygens each have minus one, giving the ion's total

00:02:32.636 --> 00:02:33.296
minus two.

00:02:34.016 --> 00:02:37.856
Every proposed drawing must satisfy both the electron inventory and the net

00:02:37.856 --> 00:02:40.556
charge before its stability is compared with alternatives.

00:02:40.872 --> 00:02:46.032
Resonance contributors keep atomic positions and connectivity unchanged while

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:47.192
changing electron placement.

00:02:48.312 --> 00:02:51.572
They are not separate molecules rapidly switching between drawings.

00:02:52.412 --> 00:02:56.209
The actual electronic structure is delocalized and cannot always be

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:56.832
represented

00:02:56.832 --> 00:02:58.792
by one localized Lewis structure.

00:02:59.932 --> 00:03:03.698
Carbonate has three equivalent contributors, each with one carbon oxygen

00:03:03.698 --> 00:03:04.012
double

00:03:04.012 --> 00:03:05.352
bond in a different position.

00:03:06.272 --> 00:03:10.492
Its three carbon oxygen bonds are equivalent in the ideal symmetric ion.

00:03:11.532 --> 00:03:15.552
The simple average Lewis bond order is four thirds, intermediate between a

00:03:15.552 --> 00:03:16.272
single and double bond.

00:03:17.412 --> 00:03:21.392
In ozone, two equivalent contributors place the double bond on opposite sides,

00:03:21.392 --> 00:03:24.212
and the simple average bond order is one point five.

00:03:25.132 --> 00:03:27.292
Resonance forms need not always contribute equally.

00:03:28.412 --> 00:03:32.095
Equivalent forms have equal weight, while non equivalent contributors differ

00:03:32.095 --> 00:03:32.192
in

00:03:32.192 --> 00:03:36.352
importance according to features such as octets, charge separation and charge

00:03:36.352 --> 00:03:36.712
placement.

00:03:37.552 --> 00:03:41.952
Moving an atom or a proton creates a different structural arrangement, not

00:03:41.952 --> 00:03:43.512
merely another resonance contributor.

00:03:44.752 --> 00:03:48.292
Curved electron arrows begin at an electron pair, not at a positive charge.

00:03:49.372 --> 00:03:53.512
Delocalization can affect bond length, stabilization and chemical reactivity.

00:03:54.532 --> 00:03:57.872
Use the drawings to explain these consequences rather than interpreting the

00:03:57.872 --> 00:04:00.632
resonance arrow as an equilibrium between isolable species.

00:04:01.272 --> 00:04:05.352
VSEPR begins with electron domains around the central atom.

00:04:06.152 --> 00:04:10.312
A multiple bond counts as one domain, while a lone pair is another domain.

00:04:11.252 --> 00:04:15.532
Two domains give a linear arrangement, three trigonal planar, and four

00:04:15.532 --> 00:04:16.112
tetrahedral.

00:04:16.852 --> 00:04:18.172
Carbon dioxide is linear.

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:23.152
Ammonia has three bond domains and one lone pair: tetrahedral electron

00:04:23.152 --> 00:04:25.812
arrangement but trigonal pyramidal molecular shape.

00:04:26.752 --> 00:04:29.672
Water has two bonds and two lone pairs and is bent.

00:04:30.472 --> 00:04:33.692
Five domains use a trigonal bipyramidal reference arrangement.

00:04:34.712 --> 00:04:39.252
In the introductory model, a lone pair prefers an equatorial site because it

00:04:39.252 --> 00:04:40.972
encounters fewer ninety degree interactions.

00:04:42.552 --> 00:04:46.472
Sulfur tetrafluoride has four bonds and one lone pair and is seesaw shaped.

00:04:47.512 --> 00:04:50.952
Chlorine trifluoride has three bonds and two lone pairs and is T shaped.

00:04:51.912 --> 00:04:55.292
Xenon difluoride has two bonds and three lone pairs and is linear.

00:04:56.212 --> 00:04:58.972
Six domains use an octahedral reference arrangement.

00:04:59.912 --> 00:05:04.212
Sulfur hexafluoride is octahedral; xenon tetrafluoride has four bonds and two

00:05:04.212 --> 00:05:06.412
opposite lone pairs and is square planar.

00:05:07.572 --> 00:05:09.352
These shape rules are useful models.

00:05:10.272 --> 00:05:13.992
Exact bond angles and lengths depend on the species, and a shape name alone

00:05:13.992 --> 00:05:18.352
does not prove a literal d orbital hybridization mechanism in hypervalent

00:05:18.352 --> 00:05:18.652
bonding.

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:23.260
A polar bond does not automatically make the entire molecule polar.

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:27.640
Bond dipoles must be combined with directions and molecular geometry.

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:33.480
Carbon dioxide has polar carbon oxygen bonds, but in the ideal linear molecule

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:36.300
the equal opposite contributions cancel.

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:39.680
Bent water does not have this cancellation.

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:45.140
Trigonal planar boron trifluoride and tetrahedral carbon tetrachloride are

00:05:45.140 --> 00:05:48.980
other familiar symmetric examples with zero net permanent molecular dipole.

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:54.600
Replacing one terminal chlorine in carbon tetrachloride by hydrogen breaks the

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:57.860
symmetry; chloroform has a nonzero molecular dipole.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:02.360
Lone pairs can influence both geometry and the full charge distribution.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:07.300
Ammonia and nitrogen trifluoride are both pyramidal, but their molecular

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:11.420
dipoles differ because the bond contributions align differently with the

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:12.740
overall electronic distribution.

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:18.300
Do not rank dipoles solely by central atom electronegativity or by counting

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:19.000
polar bonds.

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:23.840
For two equal dipole vectors separated by one hundred eighty degrees, the sum

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:24.420
is zero.

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:28.380
If the angle is smaller, the resultant generally is not zero.

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:32.217
Molecular dipole is an observable property of the complete charge

00:06:32.217 --> 00:06:32.780
distribution;

00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:36.860
individual bond arrows provide an approximate explanatory model.

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:41.100
Always establish the actual shape before claiming cancellation.

00:06:41.328 --> 00:06:46.548
In valence bond language, head on overlap along the internuclear axis makes a

00:06:46.548 --> 00:06:49.628
sigma bond, while side on overlap makes a pi bond.

00:06:50.388 --> 00:06:55.448
An ordinary double bond has one sigma and one pi bond; a triple bond has one

00:06:55.448 --> 00:06:56.608
sigma and two pi bonds.

00:06:57.568 --> 00:07:00.868
Count every bond in the whole molecule, including those to hydrogen.

00:07:01.968 --> 00:07:06.468
Ethene has four carbon hydrogen sigma bonds and one carbon carbon sigma bond,

00:07:06.768 --> 00:07:07.888
plus one pi bond.

00:07:08.488 --> 00:07:10.688
Its total is five sigma and one pi.

00:07:11.468 --> 00:07:15.828
Each carbon is described by three sp two hybrid orbitals in a planar

00:07:15.828 --> 00:07:19.668
arrangement, with an unhybridized p orbital forming the pi overlap.

00:07:19.668 --> 00:07:24.968
Ethyne has two carbon hydrogen sigma bonds and one carbon carbon sigma bond,

00:07:25.408 --> 00:07:26.328
plus two pi bonds.

00:07:26.808 --> 00:07:28.988
Its total is three sigma and two pi.

00:07:29.688 --> 00:07:32.688
Its carbons are described as sp hybridized and linear.

00:07:33.648 --> 00:07:38.068
Methane is described using sp three hybrids in a tetrahedral arrangement.

00:07:38.828 --> 00:07:43.168
Rotation that destroys a pi overlap is energetically restricted, unlike the

00:07:43.168 --> 00:07:46.348
simplified picture of free rotation about an isolated sigma bond.

00:07:47.308 --> 00:07:50.985
Hybridization is a localized model connecting orbital combinations with

00:07:50.985 --> 00:07:51.348
bonding

00:07:51.348 --> 00:07:55.648
patterns, not a directly measured label that independently proves every

00:07:55.648 --> 00:07:56.508
molecular geometry.

00:07:56.784 --> 00:08:00.044
Molecular orbitals extend across a molecule.

00:08:00.824 --> 00:08:05.064
Compatible atomic wavefunctions combine into bonding and antibonding

00:08:05.064 --> 00:08:05.724
combinations.

00:08:07.044 --> 00:08:10.600
Fill these orbitals according to their energies, Pauli's limit and Hund's

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:10.844
rule.

00:08:11.844 --> 00:08:15.284
Bond order is half the difference between bonding and antibonding electron

00:08:15.284 --> 00:08:15.664
counts.

00:08:16.544 --> 00:08:20.904
Hydrogen molecule has two bonding electrons and no antibonding electrons,

00:08:21.484 --> 00:08:22.564
giving bond order one.

00:08:23.024 --> 00:08:27.344
The elementary helium molecule configuration fills both corresponding orbitals

00:08:27.344 --> 00:08:33.164
and has bond order zero, so that model predicts no ordinary stable covalent

00:08:33.164 --> 00:08:33.904
helium dimer.

00:08:34.584 --> 00:08:38.684
Weakly bound helium pairs involve physics beyond this simple bonding picture.

00:08:39.604 --> 00:08:43.824
Oxygen has two unpaired electrons in degenerate pi antibonding orbitals,

00:08:44.764 --> 00:08:45.924
explaining its paramagnetism.

00:08:46.444 --> 00:08:47.804
Its bond order is two.

00:08:47.804 --> 00:08:53.224
Removing one antibonding electron to make oxygen molecular cation raises bond

00:08:53.224 --> 00:08:56.484
order to two point five and leaves one unpaired electron.

00:08:57.324 --> 00:09:01.604
Adding one to make superoxide lowers bond order to one point five and leaves

00:09:01.604 --> 00:09:02.824
one unpaired electron.

00:09:03.744 --> 00:09:07.944
Adding two to make peroxide gives bond order one with the relevant electrons

00:09:07.944 --> 00:09:08.304
paired.

00:09:09.124 --> 00:09:13.124
Within this related series, greater bond order generally correlates with

00:09:13.124 --> 00:09:14.124
shorter and stronger bonds.

00:09:14.684 --> 00:09:19.484
Orbital energy ordering differs among diatomic molecules, so do not copy one

00:09:19.484 --> 00:09:22.604
molecular orbital diagram blindly onto every species.

00:09:23.136 --> 00:09:26.756
Hydrogen bonding requires an appropriate donor and acceptor.

00:09:27.276 --> 00:09:31.836
In common introductory examples, a hydrogen bonded to nitrogen, oxygen or

00:09:31.836 --> 00:09:36.156
fluorine interacts with a suitable lone pair on another electronegative atom.

00:09:36.936 --> 00:09:40.929
Do not assume that every hydrogen atom or every lone pair is equally

00:09:40.929 --> 00:09:41.516
effective.

00:09:42.556 --> 00:09:47.056
Water can both donate and accept hydrogen bonds and forms an extended network.

00:09:47.496 --> 00:09:51.796
This helps explain its unusually high boiling point relative to comparable

00:09:51.796 --> 00:09:55.116
small hydrides and the open structure of ordinary ice.

00:09:56.036 --> 00:09:58.816
Intermolecular hydrogen bonds link different molecules.

00:09:59.536 --> 00:10:03.736
Intramolecular hydrogen bonds form within one molecule and may compete with

00:10:03.736 --> 00:10:05.856
interactions with neighbours or solvent.

00:10:06.356 --> 00:10:11.156
Compare ethanol and dimethyl ether: both have two carbons, six hydrogens and

00:10:11.156 --> 00:10:16.156
one oxygen, but ethanol has an oxygen hydrogen donor while dimethyl ether does

00:10:16.156 --> 00:10:16.416
not.

00:10:17.296 --> 00:10:20.976
Ether can accept hydrogen bonds from water but cannot form the same self

00:10:20.976 --> 00:10:22.896
associated donor network as ethanol.

00:10:23.816 --> 00:10:26.416
Ethanol consequently has the higher normal boiling point.

00:10:27.376 --> 00:10:31.956
Solubility and boiling point also depend on molecular size, shape, dispersion

00:10:31.956 --> 00:10:36.196
forces and other interactions, so hydrogen bonding is not the only variable.

00:10:36.776 --> 00:10:41.256
Use the twelve original questions to review electron counts, shapes, dipoles

00:10:41.456 --> 00:10:42.276
and orbital models.

00:10:43.056 --> 00:10:46.396
Further lattice cycles and complete molecular orbital diagrams remain useful

00:10:46.396 --> 00:10:46.856
practice.

00:10:47.400 --> 00:10:52.315
A Born Haber cycle relates formation of an ionic solid to a sequence of

00:10:52.315 --> 00:10:52.800
gaseous

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:53.940
atom and ion steps.

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:59.000
Use the supplied illustrative sodium chloride data in kilojoules per mole:

00:11:00.060 --> 00:11:05.140
sodium sublimation plus one hundred eight, sodium ionization plus four hundred

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:09.920
ninety six, half the chlorine bond dissociation plus one hundred twenty two,

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:13.060
and chlorine electron gain minus three hundred forty nine.

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:18.060
Suppose solid formation from the elements is minus four hundred eleven.

00:11:18.060 --> 00:11:21.740
The nonlattice steps sum to plus three hundred seventy seven, so lattice

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:25.100
formation must be minus seven hundred eighty eight to close the cycle.

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:30.440
This is the enthalpy for gaseous sodium and chloride ions forming solid sodium

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:31.540
chloride.

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:36.045
Reversing that process gives lattice dissociation plus seven hundred eighty

00:11:36.045 --> 00:11:36.500
eight.

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:40.440
Some tables use the opposite lattice convention, so copy the defining reaction

00:11:40.440 --> 00:11:41.240
before the sign.

00:11:41.960 --> 00:11:46.660
The chlorine contribution is half a mole of diatomic molecules for one mole of

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:50.800
salt; using the full dissociation value would double that step incorrectly.

00:11:51.780 --> 00:11:55.600
The cycle uses Hess's law, not a new independent empirical sign rule.

00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:59.980
Check both the balanced overall reaction and the physical states of every

00:11:59.980 --> 00:12:00.460
intermediate.

00:12:00.912 --> 00:12:04.932
Removing an electron does not always strengthen a chemical bond.

00:12:05.672 --> 00:12:09.732
The result depends on whether that electron occupied a bonding or an

00:12:09.732 --> 00:12:11.192
antibonding molecular orbital.

00:12:12.072 --> 00:12:17.292
In the elementary nitrogen molecule diagram, nitrogen has bond order three and

00:12:17.292 --> 00:12:20.652
its highest occupied orbital is a sigma bonding orbital.

00:12:21.712 --> 00:12:26.252
Removing one electron to form the nitrogen molecular cation lowers bond order

00:12:26.252 --> 00:12:29.072
to two point five and leaves an unpaired electron.

00:12:29.912 --> 00:12:34.472
Oxygen starts with bond order two and two unpaired electrons in the degenerate

00:12:34.472 --> 00:12:35.872
pi antibonding set.

00:12:36.852 --> 00:12:40.799
Removing one of those antibonding electrons raises bond order to two point

00:12:40.799 --> 00:12:41.012
five

00:12:41.012 --> 00:12:43.012
and leaves one unpaired electron.

00:12:43.892 --> 00:12:48.752
Thus the same operation, ionization, produces opposite bond order changes in

00:12:48.752 --> 00:12:49.612
these two examples.

00:12:50.192 --> 00:12:54.572
Their equal final bond orders do not prove identical bond lengths or bond

00:12:54.572 --> 00:12:57.712
energies, because the atoms and orbital energies differ.

00:12:58.232 --> 00:13:03.001
For a given related molecular series, bond order often helps compare length

00:13:03.001 --> 00:13:03.192
and

00:13:03.192 --> 00:13:07.172
strength, but it is not a universal numerical conversion between different

00:13:07.172 --> 00:13:07.572
elements.

00:13:08.812 --> 00:13:12.732
State the appropriate orbital energy ordering, locate the electron being

00:13:12.732 --> 00:13:17.352
removed, and then recount bonding, antibonding and unpaired electrons before

00:13:17.352 --> 00:13:19.072
assigning stability or magnetism.

00:13:19.272 --> 00:13:23.832
Molecular shape describes the positions of atoms, while electron domain

00:13:23.832 --> 00:13:25.872
geometry includes lone pairs.

00:13:26.892 --> 00:13:31.772
Sulfur tetrafluoride has four bonding domains and one lone pair in the

00:13:31.772 --> 00:13:33.212
elementary valence shell model.

00:13:34.172 --> 00:13:36.812
Five domains adopt a trigonal bipyramidal arrangement.

00:13:37.872 --> 00:13:41.324
Placing the lone pair in an equatorial site reduces the number of ninety

00:13:41.324 --> 00:13:41.612
degree

00:13:41.612 --> 00:13:44.592
interactions, leaving a seesaw arrangement of atoms.

00:13:45.312 --> 00:13:49.772
Chlorine trifluoride has three bonds and two lone pairs, again five domains.

00:13:50.432 --> 00:13:54.832
The two lone pairs preferentially occupy equatorial sites, leaving a T shaped

00:13:54.832 --> 00:13:55.672
atomic arrangement.

00:13:56.612 --> 00:14:00.932
Xenon tetrafluoride instead has six domains: four bonds and two lone pairs.

00:14:01.552 --> 00:14:05.318
An octahedral domain arrangement with the lone pairs opposite each other

00:14:05.318 --> 00:14:05.632
leaves

00:14:05.632 --> 00:14:07.712
four fluorine atoms in one square plane.

00:14:08.372 --> 00:14:12.392
All three molecules have different domain and atomic descriptions; counting

00:14:12.392 --> 00:14:13.912
bonds alone cannot distinguish them.

00:14:14.652 --> 00:14:18.572
These are qualitative valence shell geometries, and actual bond angles can

00:14:18.572 --> 00:14:19.852
deviate from ideal drawings.

00:14:20.692 --> 00:14:24.932
Use a valid electron count and molecular charge before assigning the number of

00:14:24.932 --> 00:14:25.212
lone pairs.

00:14:25.852 --> 00:14:29.852
A drawing should label lone pairs separately from atoms so an electron domain

00:14:29.852 --> 00:14:32.652
diagram is not mistaken for the observed molecular shape.

00:14:32.928 --> 00:14:37.988
Resonance contributors represent one delocalized electronic structure, not

00:14:37.988 --> 00:14:40.488
molecules rapidly switching between different drawings.

00:14:41.228 --> 00:14:45.688
In nitrate, three equivalent oxygen positions can share the double bond in the

00:14:45.688 --> 00:14:47.328
simplest equivalent Lewis contributors.

00:14:48.128 --> 00:14:52.828
Each contributor has one double and two single nitrogen oxygen bonds, so the

00:14:52.828 --> 00:14:55.988
total Lewis bond order across those three links is four.

00:14:56.448 --> 00:14:59.128
The average for each equivalent link is four thirds.

00:14:59.528 --> 00:15:04.033
In nitrite, the two equivalent oxygen positions share one single and one

00:15:04.033 --> 00:15:04.408
double

00:15:04.408 --> 00:15:08.368
link in the elementary contributors, giving average one point five.

00:15:08.908 --> 00:15:13.108
These bookkeeping averages are useful descriptions, not a promise that bond

00:15:13.108 --> 00:15:15.888
order is always an exactly measured fractional observable.

00:15:16.808 --> 00:15:19.508
Equivalent atom positions and contributor weights matter.

00:15:20.248 --> 00:15:24.088
For unequally weighted contributors, taking a simple unweighted average can

00:15:24.088 --> 00:15:24.488
mislead.

00:15:25.048 --> 00:15:29.564
Also keep the overall ionic charge fixed while moving electrons; resonance

00:15:29.564 --> 00:15:29.808
does

00:15:29.808 --> 00:15:32.868
not move the nuclei or create a different atom connectivity.

00:15:33.828 --> 00:15:38.048
Formal charges in individual nitrate contributors add to minus one even though

00:15:38.048 --> 00:15:39.228
their distribution changes.

00:15:40.228 --> 00:15:43.668
Compare equivalent bonds within the same species and distinguish an average

00:15:43.668 --> 00:15:48.288
resonance representation from assigning one permanently short double bond and

00:15:48.288 --> 00:15:50.148
separate permanently long single bonds.

00:15:50.784 --> 00:15:56.644
A molecular dipole is a vector sum, so equal bond dipoles do not automatically

00:15:56.644 --> 00:15:56.984
cancel.

00:15:57.864 --> 00:16:01.604
Consider a simple two bond model in which the vectors have equal magnitude mu

00:16:01.604 --> 00:16:03.224
and included angle theta.

00:16:04.264 --> 00:16:08.324
Adding their components along the angle bisector gives resultant two times mu

00:16:08.324 --> 00:16:10.104
times the cosine of half theta.

00:16:10.924 --> 00:16:14.144
At one hundred eighty degrees, the equal opposing vectors cancel.

00:16:14.724 --> 00:16:19.084
At one hundred twenty degrees, cosine sixty is one half, so the resultant

00:16:19.084 --> 00:16:21.204
equals one bond dipole rather than zero.

00:16:22.024 --> 00:16:24.984
At ninety degrees, the magnitude is square root two times mu.

00:16:26.204 --> 00:16:30.124
These comparisons use the specified vector model; they are not an exact method

00:16:30.124 --> 00:16:34.004
for predicting every molecule's measured dipole moment from an isolated bond

00:16:34.004 --> 00:16:34.304
table.

00:16:35.704 --> 00:16:38.853
Lone pairs and the full electron distribution can affect real molecular

00:16:38.853 --> 00:16:39.164
values.

00:16:39.564 --> 00:16:44.184
A symmetric molecule with several bonds may cancel all vector components, but

00:16:44.184 --> 00:16:47.304
the actual geometry and identities must support that cancellation.

00:16:48.864 --> 00:16:53.124
Draw arrows consistently and specify whether a chemistry dipole arrow or the

00:16:53.124 --> 00:16:55.844
physical electric dipole vector convention is being used.

00:16:57.384 --> 00:17:00.784
Reversing all arrows together preserves the calculated magnitude, while

00:17:00.784 --> 00:17:02.624
reversing just one changes the model.

00:17:02.784 --> 00:17:07.424
A Born Haber cycle for a divalent metal chloride must account for the full

00:17:07.424 --> 00:17:08.144
ionic formula.

00:17:09.264 --> 00:17:12.864
Use supplied illustrative energy terms for forming one mole of magnesium

00:17:12.864 --> 00:17:16.164
chloride solid from magnesium solid and chlorine gas.

00:17:17.144 --> 00:17:21.384
Magnesium atomization is plus one hundred forty eight kilojoules per mole, the

00:17:21.384 --> 00:17:25.704
first and second magnesium ionizations are plus seven hundred thirty eight and

00:17:25.704 --> 00:17:30.144
plus fourteen hundred fifty one, and converting one chlorine molecule into two

00:17:30.144 --> 00:17:33.564
gas atoms costs plus two hundred forty three.

00:17:33.564 --> 00:17:37.704
Each chlorine atom gains one electron with energy change minus three hundred

00:17:37.704 --> 00:17:39.744
forty nine, so that term occurs twice.

00:17:40.564 --> 00:17:44.084
These steps before lattice formation sum to plus eighteen hundred eighty two

00:17:44.084 --> 00:17:44.944
kilojoules per mole.

00:17:45.804 --> 00:17:50.164
If the supplied overall formation enthalpy is minus six hundred forty two, the

00:17:50.164 --> 00:17:53.404
lattice formation enthalpy is minus twenty five hundred twenty four kilojoules

00:17:53.404 --> 00:17:53.844
per mole.

00:17:54.584 --> 00:17:58.758
The corresponding lattice dissociation value has the opposite sign for the

00:17:58.758 --> 00:17:58.984
same

00:17:58.984 --> 00:17:59.284
states.

00:18:00.444 --> 00:18:03.544
Using only the first magnesium ionization would leave the metal charge wrong.

00:18:04.524 --> 00:18:07.724
Using only one chlorine electron gain would fail the formula count.

00:18:08.784 --> 00:18:12.515
Label initial and final states and write the energy equation before solving

00:18:12.515 --> 00:18:12.664
for

00:18:12.664 --> 00:18:13.284
the missing term.

00:18:14.448 --> 00:18:19.068
A small change in ionic charge can change both electron count and molecular

00:18:19.068 --> 00:18:19.428
shape.

00:18:20.168 --> 00:18:24.988
For the nitrite ion, nitrogen contributes five valence electrons, two oxygens

00:18:24.988 --> 00:18:29.128
contribute twelve, and the negative charge adds one, giving eighteen.

00:18:29.128 --> 00:18:33.916
In the ordinary octet Lewis description, nitrogen has two oxygen neighbours

00:18:33.916 --> 00:18:34.108
and

00:18:34.108 --> 00:18:34.848
one lone pair.

00:18:35.468 --> 00:18:39.328
One double and one single bond can be drawn in either of two equivalent

00:18:39.328 --> 00:18:40.268
resonance contributors.

00:18:40.918 --> 00:18:45.108
Three electron domains around nitrogen give a bent molecular shape, while

00:18:45.108 --> 00:18:48.868
resonance makes the equivalent oxygen positions share the bonding description.

00:18:49.628 --> 00:18:54.008
The nitronium ion has the same atom count but two fewer electrons because its

00:18:54.008 --> 00:18:55.768
charge is positive rather than negative.

00:18:55.768 --> 00:19:00.348
Sixteen valence electrons support the familiar two double bond Lewis

00:19:00.348 --> 00:19:02.788
arrangement with no central nitrogen lone pair.

00:19:03.488 --> 00:19:05.848
Two electron domains give a linear molecular shape.

00:19:06.468 --> 00:19:08.788
A double bond counts as one domain for this purpose.

00:19:09.188 --> 00:19:13.803
Do not confuse either closed shell ion with neutral nitrogen dioxide, which

00:19:13.803 --> 00:19:13.988
has

00:19:13.988 --> 00:19:16.528
seventeen valence electrons and an odd electron.

00:19:17.368 --> 00:19:20.888
Count charge before applying a memorized shape or copying a Lewis diagram.

00:19:21.808 --> 00:19:25.470
Geometry follows the relevant electronic description, not the atom formula

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:25.668
with

00:19:25.668 --> 00:19:26.828
the charge silently omitted.

00:19:27.096 --> 00:19:31.350
Average bond enthalpies estimate reaction energy by breaking gas phase

00:19:31.350 --> 00:19:31.836
reactant

00:19:31.836 --> 00:19:34.076
bonds and forming gas phase product bonds.

00:19:35.156 --> 00:19:37.236
Consider ethene plus hydrogen giving ethane.

00:19:37.996 --> 00:19:42.176
Use supplied average values in kilojoules per mole: carbon carbon double bond

00:19:42.176 --> 00:19:47.256
six hundred fourteen, hydrogen hydrogen four hundred thirty six, carbon carbon

00:19:47.256 --> 00:19:51.889
single bond three hundred forty seven, and carbon hydrogen four hundred

00:19:51.889 --> 00:19:52.556
thirteen.

00:19:52.556 --> 00:19:56.043
Four carbon hydrogen bonds occur on each side and cancel from a net

00:19:56.043 --> 00:19:56.616
bookkeeping

00:19:56.616 --> 00:19:57.016
list.

00:19:57.776 --> 00:20:01.496
The changed bond set breaks one carbon carbon double bond and one hydrogen

00:20:01.496 --> 00:20:05.076
hydrogen bond, costing ten hundred fifty kilojoules per mole.

00:20:05.776 --> 00:20:09.576
It forms one carbon carbon single bond and two additional carbon hydrogen

00:20:09.576 --> 00:20:12.296
bonds, releasing eleven hundred seventy three.

00:20:12.296 --> 00:20:16.096
The estimated net is minus one hundred twenty three kilojoules per mole.

00:20:17.116 --> 00:20:20.776
Forgetting the retained sigma bond in the product or subtracting all product

00:20:20.776 --> 00:20:22.956
energy with the wrong sign changes the result.

00:20:23.936 --> 00:20:27.476
Average bond values depend on molecular environment and do not make this an

00:20:27.476 --> 00:20:29.236
exact enthalpy of hydrogenation.

00:20:29.816 --> 00:20:33.456
Liquid and solid phase changes need separate terms if the reaction states

00:20:33.456 --> 00:20:34.876
differ from the gas phase model.

00:20:35.856 --> 00:20:39.596
State the bond inventory and the approximation before interpreting the sign.

00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:44.600
Different atoms in a diatomic molecule require more care than copying every

00:20:44.600 --> 00:20:46.720
feature of a homonuclear orbital diagram.

00:20:47.780 --> 00:20:51.940
Carbon monoxide has ten valence electrons, while nitric oxide has eleven.

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:56.800
In the introductory molecular orbital counting model, carbon monoxide has bond

00:20:56.800 --> 00:20:59.060
order three and all electrons paired.

00:20:59.900 --> 00:21:04.380
Nitric oxide has one electron in an antibonding pi orbital, giving bond order

00:21:04.380 --> 00:21:07.180
two point five and one unpaired electron.

00:21:07.980 --> 00:21:10.800
It is therefore paramagnetic in this elementary comparison.

00:21:12.140 --> 00:21:16.182
Removing that antibonding electron from nitric oxide gives the nitrosonium

00:21:16.182 --> 00:21:16.400
ion,

00:21:16.900 --> 00:21:21.440
with ten valence electrons, bond order three and a paired configuration in the

00:21:21.440 --> 00:21:21.920
same model.

00:21:22.780 --> 00:21:26.780
The general counting expression is one half the bonding minus antibonding

00:21:26.780 --> 00:21:27.800
electron populations.

00:21:27.800 --> 00:21:33.240
However, heteronuclear atomic orbitals begin at unequal energies, and the

00:21:33.240 --> 00:21:37.020
resulting molecular orbitals need not have equal contributions on both atoms.

00:21:37.960 --> 00:21:42.400
Electron count alone therefore does not prove equal dipole moments, identical

00:21:42.400 --> 00:21:45.740
orbital energies or identical bond lengths for different molecules.

00:21:46.280 --> 00:21:50.880
This chapter supplies an introductory population comparison, not a complete

00:21:50.880 --> 00:21:52.460
heteronuclear orbital derivation.

00:21:53.280 --> 00:21:57.099
Use the stated filling model and identify the orbital from which an electron

00:21:57.099 --> 00:21:57.200
is

00:21:57.200 --> 00:22:00.960
removed rather than assuming every ionization weakens every bond.

00:22:01.272 --> 00:22:05.552
The relative order of sigma and pi molecular orbitals is not identical for

00:22:05.552 --> 00:22:07.552
every second period diatomic molecule.

00:22:08.312 --> 00:22:12.872
In the introductory valence orbital diagram for boron two, carbon two and

00:22:12.872 --> 00:22:17.532
nitrogen two, the bonding pi two p pair lies below the bonding sigma two p

00:22:17.532 --> 00:22:17.772
orbital.

00:22:18.612 --> 00:22:23.312
The filled sigma two s and sigma star two s orbitals contribute equal bonding

00:22:23.312 --> 00:22:26.392
and antibonding populations, cancelling in the bond order.

00:22:27.192 --> 00:22:29.112
Boron two has six valence electrons.

00:22:29.792 --> 00:22:33.992
Its final two occupy the two degenerate bonding pi orbitals singly with

00:22:33.992 --> 00:22:37.872
parallel spins, giving bond order one and two unpaired electrons.

00:22:38.452 --> 00:22:39.912
It is paramagnetic in this model.

00:22:40.872 --> 00:22:44.932
Carbon two has eight valence electrons and fills both pi orbitals, giving bond

00:22:44.932 --> 00:22:46.732
order two with all electrons paired.

00:22:47.512 --> 00:22:51.497
Nitrogen two adds two electrons to the bonding sigma two p orbital, giving

00:22:51.497 --> 00:22:51.712
bond

00:22:51.712 --> 00:22:53.552
order three and a paired configuration.

00:22:54.152 --> 00:22:57.512
Filled core orbitals have been omitted because their bonding contributions

00:22:57.512 --> 00:22:58.332
cancel here.

00:22:59.012 --> 00:23:02.472
Do not transfer the oxygen two orbital ordering unchanged to these three

00:23:02.472 --> 00:23:02.852
molecules.

00:23:03.692 --> 00:23:07.312
Use the appropriate energy order, Pauli exclusion and Hund's rule together

00:23:07.312 --> 00:23:09.732
before assigning bond order or magnetism.

00:23:10.632 --> 00:23:15.052
A coordinate bond describes the origin of an electron pair in a bond forming

00:23:15.052 --> 00:23:15.532
step.

00:23:16.532 --> 00:23:20.072
Ammonia has a nitrogen lone pair and can act as a Lewis base.

00:23:20.852 --> 00:23:24.832
In the simple Lewis structure of boron trifluoride, boron has only six

00:23:24.832 --> 00:23:27.992
electrons around it and can accept a pair as a Lewis acid.

00:23:28.912 --> 00:23:33.272
Donation from nitrogen to boron gives the ammonia boron trifluoride adduct.

00:23:34.172 --> 00:23:38.852
The donor arrow points from nitrogen toward boron; it does not represent a

00:23:38.852 --> 00:23:39.252
proton transfer.

00:23:39.252 --> 00:23:44.546
In the resulting single bond Lewis drawing, nitrogen has four bonds and no

00:23:44.546 --> 00:23:44.832
lone

00:23:44.832 --> 00:23:48.672
pair, so its formal charge is five minus four, or plus one.

00:23:49.832 --> 00:23:53.532
Boron also has four bonds, giving three minus four, or minus one.

00:23:54.212 --> 00:23:55.852
The total adduct remains neutral.

00:23:56.772 --> 00:24:00.812
These formal charges are electron bookkeeping, not proof of complete ionic

00:24:00.812 --> 00:24:02.912
separation or measured atomic charges.

00:24:03.392 --> 00:24:07.472
Around each bonded nitrogen and boron centre there are four bond domains,

00:24:08.112 --> 00:24:11.792
approximately tetrahedral rather than the original trigonal planar boron

00:24:11.792 --> 00:24:12.172
arrangement.

00:24:13.092 --> 00:24:16.552
No new electrons were created: the nitrogen pair became shared.

00:24:17.372 --> 00:24:21.536
After formation, the bond is a shared electron pair interaction, not a

00:24:21.536 --> 00:24:22.012
separate

00:24:22.012 --> 00:24:25.112
physical class exempt from ordinary bonding principles.

00:24:25.488 --> 00:24:30.288
Hydrogen bonding can link molecules or connect suitable sites within one

00:24:30.288 --> 00:24:30.648
molecule.

00:24:31.508 --> 00:24:36.049
In two nitrophenol, the hydroxyl group and neighbouring nitro group can form

00:24:36.049 --> 00:24:36.168
an

00:24:36.168 --> 00:24:40.768
intramolecular hydrogen bond from the hydroxyl hydrogen to a nitro oxygen.

00:24:41.648 --> 00:24:44.828
The nearby positions permit a favourable internal arrangement.

00:24:45.628 --> 00:24:49.448
In four nitrophenol, the para positions do not allow that same local

00:24:49.448 --> 00:24:53.208
connection, and intermolecular hydrogen bonding becomes important.

00:24:53.508 --> 00:24:58.448
The difference affects association between molecules and helps explain why the

00:24:58.448 --> 00:25:03.128
ortho isomer is more steam volatile in the familiar separation comparison.

00:25:04.568 --> 00:25:08.668
This does not mean that an internally hydrogen bonded molecule has no

00:25:08.668 --> 00:25:11.108
interactions with water or with other molecules.

00:25:11.888 --> 00:25:16.439
Nor does one hydrogen bond label uniquely determine every solubility or

00:25:16.439 --> 00:25:16.888
melting

00:25:16.888 --> 00:25:17.248
point.

00:25:18.088 --> 00:25:21.948
Crystal packing, molecular shape, solvent and temperature also matter.

00:25:22.628 --> 00:25:27.307
Identify the donor and acceptor explicitly: a hydroxyl group supplies the

00:25:27.307 --> 00:25:27.628
donor

00:25:27.628 --> 00:25:31.468
hydrogen, while a suitable nitro oxygen acts as acceptor.

00:25:32.108 --> 00:25:36.768
The nitro group contains no nitrogen hydrogen donor simply because nitrogen is

00:25:36.768 --> 00:25:37.048
present.

00:25:38.128 --> 00:25:42.088
Compare the geometry and competing interactions before turning a structural

00:25:42.088 --> 00:25:44.728
observation into a physical property prediction.

00:25:45.048 --> 00:25:49.628
A reliable sigma and pi count begins with the molecular connectivity.

00:25:50.588 --> 00:25:54.588
Every bonded atom pair has one sigma connection in the elementary localized

00:25:54.588 --> 00:25:55.048
description.

00:25:55.728 --> 00:26:00.268
A double bond contributes one additional pi bond and a triple bond contributes

00:26:00.268 --> 00:26:00.688
two.

00:26:01.478 --> 00:26:06.088
Ethyne has two carbon hydrogen sigma bonds and one carbon carbon sigma bond,

00:26:06.528 --> 00:26:09.248
giving three sigma and two pi bonds altogether.

00:26:09.948 --> 00:26:14.808
Now read the structure of acrylonitrile as a carbon bearing two hydrogens,

00:26:15.248 --> 00:26:19.748
double bonded to a carbon bearing one hydrogen, then single bonded to a carbon

00:26:19.988 --> 00:26:21.608
which is triple bonded to nitrogen.

00:26:22.048 --> 00:26:26.228
There are three carbon hydrogen connections and three connections along the

00:26:26.228 --> 00:26:28.688
heavy atom chain, giving six sigma bonds.

00:26:29.268 --> 00:26:33.608
The carbon carbon double bond supplies one pi bond and the nitrile supplies

00:26:33.608 --> 00:26:35.248
two, for three pi bonds.

00:26:35.808 --> 00:26:41.008
In benzene, six ring connections and six carbon hydrogen bonds give twelve

00:26:41.008 --> 00:26:41.648
sigma bonds.

00:26:42.428 --> 00:26:46.428
A drawing with alternating single and double bonds contains three formal pi

00:26:46.428 --> 00:26:51.668
bonds, but the actual six pi electrons are delocalized over the ring rather

00:26:51.668 --> 00:26:54.608
than confined permanently to three selected links.

00:26:55.588 --> 00:26:59.308
Count implicit hydrogens and distinguish an electron count from a bond count.

00:26:59.728 --> 00:27:04.208
A structural drawing is essential; molecular formula alone need not determine

00:27:04.208 --> 00:27:05.488
the arrangement of all bonds.

00:27:05.856 --> 00:27:10.576
A heteronuclear molecular orbital diagram must respect orbital symmetry and

00:27:10.576 --> 00:27:12.056
unequal atomic energies.

00:27:12.916 --> 00:27:15.456
Take the hydrogen fluoride bond as the z axis.

00:27:16.196 --> 00:27:20.936
In a supplied simplified valence model, hydrogen one s interacts most usefully

00:27:20.936 --> 00:27:25.636
with fluorine two p z to form a sigma bonding and a sigma antibonding orbital.

00:27:26.276 --> 00:27:29.902
The perpendicular fluorine two p x and two p y orbitals have the wrong

00:27:29.902 --> 00:27:30.316
symmetry

00:27:30.316 --> 00:27:34.976
for this overlap with hydrogen one s and are treated as nonbonding.

00:27:34.976 --> 00:27:39.996
The much deeper fluorine two s level is also treated as largely nonbonding in

00:27:39.996 --> 00:27:40.996
this introductory model.

00:27:42.016 --> 00:27:44.996
Hydrogen contributes one valence electron and fluorine seven.

00:27:45.836 --> 00:27:49.936
Place two in the low fluorine two s derived level, two in the sigma bond and

00:27:49.936 --> 00:27:52.596
four across the two perpendicular nonbonding orbitals.

00:27:53.496 --> 00:27:54.976
Sigma star remains empty.

00:27:55.656 --> 00:28:00.516
The bonding minus antibonding count divided by two gives bond order one, and

00:28:00.516 --> 00:28:04.096
every occupied orbital is paired, consistent with diamagnetism.

00:28:04.816 --> 00:28:08.516
The occupied molecular orbitals need not contain equal hydrogen and fluorine

00:28:08.516 --> 00:28:09.056
contributions.

00:28:09.836 --> 00:28:13.676
The diagram is qualitative and omits core electrons and detailed mixing;

00:28:14.476 --> 00:28:18.456
homonuclear gerade and ungerade labels do not apply to this unequal atom

00:28:18.456 --> 00:28:18.876
molecule.

00:28:19.104 --> 00:28:24.224
A bond potential curve measures energy against internuclear separation, rather

00:28:24.224 --> 00:28:25.644
than plotting a reaction rate.

00:28:26.604 --> 00:28:29.564
Choose separated ground state atoms as zero potential energy.

00:28:30.564 --> 00:28:35.592
At very short distance, strong repulsion raises the curve; attraction lowers

00:28:35.592 --> 00:28:35.724
it

00:28:35.724 --> 00:28:37.724
toward a minimum at the equilibrium separation.

00:28:38.544 --> 00:28:42.224
At that minimum the slope is zero, so the net force is zero.

00:28:43.064 --> 00:28:46.024
This does not mean that separating the atoms costs no energy.

00:28:46.484 --> 00:28:51.264
The vertical depth from the minimum to separated atoms is called D e.

00:28:51.264 --> 00:28:54.924
A supporting quantum refinement recognizes that the lowest vibrational level

00:28:54.924 --> 00:28:57.584
lies above the minimum by its zero point energy.

00:28:58.604 --> 00:29:03.584
Dissociation from that level therefore requires D zero, equal to D e minus the

00:29:03.584 --> 00:29:04.584
zero point contribution.

00:29:05.544 --> 00:29:09.344
For illustrative values of four hundred fifty kilojoules per mole for the well

00:29:09.344 --> 00:29:13.836
depth and twenty five for the zero point energy, D zero is four hundred twenty

00:29:13.836 --> 00:29:14.784
five kilojoules per mole.

00:29:15.544 --> 00:29:19.784
These are supplied model values, not a measured bond assignment or an average

00:29:19.784 --> 00:29:21.904
bond enthalpy at an unspecified temperature.

00:29:22.864 --> 00:29:27.164
On the long distance side of the minimum the force attracts the atoms back; on

00:29:27.164 --> 00:29:29.404
the short distance side it pushes them apart.

00:29:29.664 --> 00:29:34.204
Insert neutral nitrogen dioxide between the familiar nitronium and nitrite

00:29:34.204 --> 00:29:34.644
ions.

00:29:35.564 --> 00:29:40.244
Nitrogen contributes five valence electrons and two oxygens contribute twelve.

00:29:40.244 --> 00:29:44.504
Removing one electron gives sixteen for nitronium, leaving seventeen for

00:29:44.504 --> 00:29:48.624
neutral nitrogen dioxide and adding one gives eighteen for nitrite.

00:29:48.904 --> 00:29:53.144
The isolated neutral molecule therefore cannot have every electron paired.

00:29:53.684 --> 00:29:56.544
Its ground state is a bent radical and is paramagnetic.

00:29:57.304 --> 00:30:01.535
Nitronium is linear in the ordinary closed shell model, whereas nitrite is

00:30:01.535 --> 00:30:01.764
bent

00:30:01.764 --> 00:30:03.064
with a central lone pair.

00:30:03.964 --> 00:30:07.764
Do not assign the neutral radical a closed shell electron pair picture merely

00:30:07.764 --> 00:30:09.504
because it shares the same atom skeleton.

00:30:10.404 --> 00:30:14.124
Nor does a one electron change simply mean that one complete bond disappears.

00:30:15.004 --> 00:30:19.584
Two nitrogen dioxide radicals can combine to form dinitrogen tetroxide, whose

00:30:19.584 --> 00:30:21.604
usual ground state has paired electrons.

00:30:22.364 --> 00:30:26.402
Their gas mixture is an equilibrium composition that depends on temperature

00:30:26.402 --> 00:30:26.564
and

00:30:26.564 --> 00:30:30.864
pressure, so a sample's magnetic or colour observation need not correspond to

00:30:30.864 --> 00:30:33.384
pure isolated nitrogen dioxide molecules alone.

00:30:34.384 --> 00:30:38.344
Counting an odd number establishes at least one unpaired electron; it does not

00:30:38.344 --> 00:30:42.184
by itself determine the exact bond angle or every detail of the molecular

00:30:42.184 --> 00:30:42.904
orbital diagram.

00:30:43.416 --> 00:30:47.682
A positional isomer comparison tests whether a vector rule survives a change

00:30:47.682 --> 00:30:48.356
in geometry.

00:30:49.296 --> 00:30:53.996
Use an explicitly idealized planar regular benzene ring with two equal outward

00:30:53.996 --> 00:30:58.316
radial carbon chlorine bond dipoles, and neglect other dipole contributions.

00:30:59.316 --> 00:31:03.596
Adjacent ortho substitution puts the two vectors sixty degrees apart, meta

00:31:03.596 --> 00:31:08.096
substitution gives one hundred twenty degrees, and opposite para substitution

00:31:08.096 --> 00:31:09.776
gives one hundred eighty degrees.

00:31:10.636 --> 00:31:14.423
The magnitude of their sum is twice the individual magnitude times the

00:31:14.423 --> 00:31:14.856
absolute

00:31:14.856 --> 00:31:16.196
cosine of half their angle.

00:31:17.036 --> 00:31:21.076
The predicted magnitudes are square root three times mu, mu, and zero,

00:31:21.316 --> 00:31:21.696
respectively.

00:31:22.816 --> 00:31:27.316
For an illustrative individual contribution of one point five zero debye, the

00:31:27.316 --> 00:31:31.876
model gives approximately two point six zero, one point five zero, and zero

00:31:31.876 --> 00:31:32.136
debye.

00:31:32.776 --> 00:31:36.196
Equal chemical bonds cancel only when their vectors oppose with matching

00:31:36.196 --> 00:31:38.956
magnitudes; their equality alone is insufficient.

00:31:38.956 --> 00:31:43.616
Para symmetry supports cancellation for the symmetric molecule, but the

00:31:43.616 --> 00:31:47.656
numerical ortho and meta estimates are model outputs, not guaranteed measured

00:31:47.656 --> 00:31:48.356
dipole moments.

00:31:49.256 --> 00:31:53.356
Real electron redistribution and geometry can modify local bond contributions.

00:31:54.476 --> 00:31:58.396
Changing one substituent also removes the equal vector assumption, so opposite

00:31:58.396 --> 00:32:00.816
placement by itself no longer guarantees cancellation.

00:32:01.368 --> 00:32:05.788
Molecular orbital construction combines wavefunctions, not coloured electric

00:32:05.788 --> 00:32:06.148
charges.

00:32:06.988 --> 00:32:10.948
Take two same phase one s atomic orbitals on equivalent centres in a

00:32:10.948 --> 00:32:12.368
qualitative diatomic model.

00:32:13.108 --> 00:32:17.748
Their sum reinforces amplitude between the nuclei and forms the usual lower

00:32:17.748 --> 00:32:19.148
energy bonding combination.

00:32:19.828 --> 00:32:24.088
Their difference cancels at the symmetry midpoint and creates a nodal plane

00:32:24.088 --> 00:32:26.488
between the nuclei in the antibonding combination.

00:32:27.068 --> 00:32:31.688
The sign of a wavefunction lobe indicates phase, not a positive or negative

00:32:31.688 --> 00:32:32.968
cloud of electron charge.

00:32:34.148 --> 00:32:37.368
Probability density is proportional to the squared magnitude of the combined

00:32:37.368 --> 00:32:40.028
wavefunction, so its interference term matters.

00:32:40.848 --> 00:32:45.628
An overall change of sign leaves the probability density unchanged; a relative

00:32:45.628 --> 00:32:49.128
sign change between the two contributions can change the interference.

00:32:50.008 --> 00:32:54.808
Proper normalization and overlap are needed for quantitative calculations, so

00:32:54.808 --> 00:32:59.628
the simple plus and minus drawings are not complete numerical wavefunctions.

00:32:59.628 --> 00:33:03.628
Two atomic basis functions generate two molecular orbital combinations in this

00:33:03.628 --> 00:33:03.808
model.

00:33:04.928 --> 00:33:08.647
Filling bonding or antibonding orbitals then affects the energy and formal

00:33:08.647 --> 00:33:08.848
bond

00:33:08.848 --> 00:33:12.788
order, rather than the act of drawing two overlapping circles proving a bond.

00:33:13.188 --> 00:33:17.669
The phase and nodal description explains the origin of the familiar bonding

00:33:17.669 --> 00:33:17.848
and

00:33:17.848 --> 00:33:18.768
antibonding labels.

00:33:18.984 --> 00:33:23.304
An electron deficient molecule can require a bonding description beyond

00:33:23.304 --> 00:33:25.464
ordinary two centre electron pairs.

00:33:26.324 --> 00:33:30.393
Diborane has two boron atoms and six hydrogens, giving twelve valence

00:33:30.393 --> 00:33:30.924
electrons

00:33:30.924 --> 00:33:31.444
in total.

00:33:32.244 --> 00:33:36.424
Four terminal boron hydrogen bonds can be counted as four ordinary two centre

00:33:36.424 --> 00:33:38.684
two electron bonds, using eight electrons.

00:33:39.344 --> 00:33:43.724
The remaining four electrons occupy two bridging boron hydrogen boron bonding

00:33:43.724 --> 00:33:47.444
units, with two electrons shared over three centres in each bridge.

00:33:48.074 --> 00:33:51.844
The two bridging hydrogens are distinct from the four terminal hydrogens.

00:33:52.884 --> 00:33:56.184
Counting each of the four bridge contacts as its own conventional two electron

00:33:56.184 --> 00:33:59.684
bond would require eight bridge electrons instead of the four available.

00:34:00.444 --> 00:34:04.604
The three centre description fixes that electron inventory problem without

00:34:04.604 --> 00:34:08.444
inserting an extra ordinary boron boron bond into the elementary ledger.

00:34:09.184 --> 00:34:13.171
It does not assign a full measured bond order or identical bond length to

00:34:13.171 --> 00:34:13.444
every

00:34:13.444 --> 00:34:14.784
terminal and bridging contact.

00:34:15.094 --> 00:34:19.104
The shape of a bridge and the distribution of its electron pair require

00:34:19.104 --> 00:34:20.364
molecular orbital reasoning.

00:34:21.244 --> 00:34:25.224
This selected compound illustrates electron deficiency and the limits of a

00:34:25.224 --> 00:34:29.664
universal octet shortcut; it is not a claim that every boron hydride has the

00:34:29.664 --> 00:34:30.444
same bridge pattern.

00:34:30.648 --> 00:34:34.748
A three centre bonding model can be electron rich rather than electron

00:34:34.748 --> 00:34:35.168
deficient.

00:34:35.848 --> 00:34:39.848
For a supporting qualitative description of linear xenon difluoride, consider

00:34:39.848 --> 00:34:42.968
the axial fluorine xenon fluorine orbital subset.

00:34:43.968 --> 00:34:48.548
Three appropriately oriented basis orbitals combine into bonding, nonbonding

00:34:48.848 --> 00:34:50.428
and antibonding molecular orbitals.

00:34:51.408 --> 00:34:55.508
Four electrons in this subset occupy the bonding level as a pair and the

00:34:55.508 --> 00:34:58.848
nonbonding level as another pair, leaving the antibonding level empty.

00:34:59.408 --> 00:35:03.308
This differs from a three centre two electron bridge, where only the bonding

00:35:03.308 --> 00:35:04.368
level is filled.

00:35:04.908 --> 00:35:09.028
In the ideal symmetric bookkeeping model, two bonding electrons and no

00:35:09.028 --> 00:35:13.348
antibonding electrons correspond to one total formal bond order distributed

00:35:13.348 --> 00:35:17.868
across two equivalent xenon fluorine links, often described as one half per

00:35:17.868 --> 00:35:18.028
link.

00:35:18.768 --> 00:35:23.008
That is a simplified model quantity, not a direct claim of an exactly measured

00:35:23.008 --> 00:35:23.548
half bond.

00:35:24.228 --> 00:35:28.714
The xenon five s lone pair, its two other p lone pairs and the remaining

00:35:28.714 --> 00:35:29.088
ligand

00:35:29.088 --> 00:35:32.008
electrons lie outside this chosen axial subset.

00:35:32.708 --> 00:35:37.190
The model explains why useful hypervalent bonding descriptions need not rely

00:35:37.190 --> 00:35:37.308
on

00:35:37.308 --> 00:35:39.088
large xenon d orbital participation.

00:35:40.148 --> 00:35:43.275
Geometry and a Lewis electron domain picture can still be discussed

00:35:43.275 --> 00:35:43.788
separately.

00:35:44.508 --> 00:35:48.608
These three energy levels are qualitative; real heteronuclear orbital energies

00:35:48.608 --> 00:35:50.708
and mixing are not equal by assumption.

00:35:50.856 --> 00:35:55.096
Resonance contributors preserve the positions and connections of nuclei.

00:35:55.956 --> 00:36:00.785
In carbonate, three symmetry related oxygen sites permit three equivalent

00:36:00.785 --> 00:36:01.116
major

00:36:01.116 --> 00:36:05.638
Lewis contributors with the carbon oxygen double bond placed at each site in

00:36:05.638 --> 00:36:05.936
turn.

00:36:06.916 --> 00:36:11.436
The simple equal contributor average gives formal bond order four thirds for

00:36:11.436 --> 00:36:12.796
each carbon oxygen link.

00:36:13.796 --> 00:36:18.036
Now attach a proton to a particular oxygen to describe hydrogen carbonate.

00:36:18.556 --> 00:36:23.104
That oxygen is the hydroxyl site, and moving the proton to another oxygen

00:36:23.104 --> 00:36:23.416
would

00:36:23.416 --> 00:36:27.176
change a nuclear connection rather than draw a resonance contributor of the

00:36:27.176 --> 00:36:28.236
same fixed structure.

00:36:29.236 --> 00:36:33.476
In the usual dominant contributor model, the double bond and negative charge

00:36:33.476 --> 00:36:36.896
are delocalized over the two nonhydroxyl oxygens.

00:36:37.656 --> 00:36:42.016
Their formal averaged bond orders are one point five each, while the hydroxyl

00:36:42.016 --> 00:36:44.536
carbon oxygen bond is represented as one.

00:36:45.336 --> 00:36:49.876
Minor charge separated contributors and the environment can change the

00:36:49.876 --> 00:36:53.458
quantitative description, so these fractions are teaching model averages

00:36:53.458 --> 00:36:53.756
rather

00:36:53.756 --> 00:36:55.376
than exact measured bond lengths.

00:36:56.556 --> 00:37:00.236
Carbonate and hydrogen carbonate are also different protonation states with

00:37:00.236 --> 00:37:01.296
different total charges.

00:37:02.476 --> 00:37:06.076
Keep proton transfer, resonance electron movement and the symmetry

00:37:06.076 --> 00:37:12.236
of

00:37:12.236 --> 00:37:12.255
the actual fixed nuclear framework separate before claiming that every oxygen

00:37:12.255 --> 00:37:12.264
bond must be equivalent.

00:37:12.264 --> 00:37:16.925
The octet rule is a useful counting guide, not a rule that every isolated

00:37:16.925 --> 00:37:17.244
Lewis

00:37:17.244 --> 00:37:19.784
drawing must obey by inventing extra electrons.

00:37:20.504 --> 00:37:24.744
In the selected gaseous monomer comparison, beryllium dichloride has two

00:37:24.744 --> 00:37:29.044
beryllium chlorine connections and only four electrons around beryllium in the

00:37:29.044 --> 00:37:29.924
simple Lewis structure.

00:37:30.764 --> 00:37:33.884
Its two bonding domains give a linear molecular model.

00:37:33.884 --> 00:37:39.004
Now compare a specified chloride donor adduct containing beryllium bonded to

00:37:39.004 --> 00:37:42.544
four chlorine atoms with overall charge two minus.

00:37:42.544 --> 00:37:45.984
Two chloride donors add two new electron pair connections to the electron

00:37:45.984 --> 00:37:47.284
deficient centre.

00:37:47.284 --> 00:37:51.164
The total valence electron count changes from sixteen in neutral beryllium

00:37:51.164 --> 00:37:54.004
dichloride to thirty two in tetrachloroberyllate.

00:37:54.244 --> 00:37:58.804
A four domain, no lone pair model at beryllium is tetrahedral, and its Lewis

00:37:58.804 --> 00:37:59.744
octet is complete.

00:37:59.744 --> 00:38:04.204
These are different chemical species and different coordination numbers, not

00:38:04.204 --> 00:38:06.164
two resonance drawings of the same molecule.

00:38:06.924 --> 00:38:10.964
The monomer description must not be applied automatically to every phase of

00:38:10.964 --> 00:38:14.084
beryllium chloride, which can associate into bridged structures.

00:38:14.884 --> 00:38:17.184
This map illustrates electron pair acceptance.

00:38:17.804 --> 00:38:21.404
It is not a preparation method and does not promise a quantitative product

00:38:21.404 --> 00:38:21.664
yield.

00:38:21.864 --> 00:38:26.404
A lattice energy trend needs a model and a sign convention before it needs

00:38:26.404 --> 00:38:26.884
arithmetic.

00:38:27.884 --> 00:38:32.284
Consider a stipulated electrostatic comparison in which all structural and

00:38:32.284 --> 00:38:33.584
repulsion factors are held the same.

00:38:34.284 --> 00:38:38.344
The magnitude of the model lattice energy is proportional to the magnitude of

00:38:38.344 --> 00:38:41.784
the ionic charge product divided by nearest neighbour separation.

00:38:42.864 --> 00:38:47.784
Let solid A have charges plus one and minus one with separation two hundred

00:38:47.784 --> 00:38:48.904
fifty picometres.

00:38:48.904 --> 00:38:54.051
Let solid B have charges plus two and minus two with separation two hundred

00:38:54.051 --> 00:38:54.744
picometres.

00:38:54.744 --> 00:38:58.266
The charge product magnitude grows from one to four, and the smaller

00:38:58.266 --> 00:38:58.784
separation

00:38:58.784 --> 00:39:02.804
adds a factor of two hundred fifty divided by two hundred.

00:39:02.804 --> 00:39:06.724
The predicted energy magnitude ratio B to A is therefore five.

00:39:07.424 --> 00:39:11.524
This is an original ideal model exercise, not a table of measured lattice

00:39:11.524 --> 00:39:13.024
enthalpies for two real salts.

00:39:13.824 --> 00:39:17.964
A formation lattice enthalpy is negative under the usual convention, whereas

00:39:17.964 --> 00:39:20.844
dissociation into gaseous ions has the opposite sign.

00:39:21.744 --> 00:39:25.804
A larger lattice energy magnitude alone also does not determine aqueous

00:39:25.804 --> 00:39:30.602
solubility, because hydration and entropy contributions must be considered in

00:39:30.602 --> 00:39:30.664
a

00:39:30.664 --> 00:39:32.044
dissolution free energy balance.

00:39:33.672 --> 00:39:38.532
Formal charge and oxidation state assign bonding electrons by different

00:39:38.532 --> 00:39:39.432
bookkeeping rules.

00:39:40.572 --> 00:39:45.012
Draw the selected octet Lewis structure of carbon monoxide with a triple bond

00:39:45.012 --> 00:39:47.032
and one lone pair on each atom.

00:39:48.172 --> 00:39:52.312
Carbon has four valence electrons in the neutral reference, two nonbonding

00:39:52.312 --> 00:39:56.452
electrons in this drawing and three electrons assigned from half of the six

00:39:56.452 --> 00:39:57.212
bonding electrons.

00:39:57.212 --> 00:39:59.632
Its formal charge is minus one.

00:40:00.552 --> 00:40:04.672
Oxygen similarly gives six minus two minus three, or plus one.

00:40:05.352 --> 00:40:08.632
The formal charges sum to zero, matching the neutral molecule.

00:40:09.812 --> 00:40:13.712
For conventional oxidation states, the heteronuclear bonding electrons are

00:40:13.712 --> 00:40:15.972
instead assigned to the more electronegative oxygen.

00:40:17.272 --> 00:40:21.012
Oxygen receives oxidation state minus two and carbon plus two.

00:40:21.692 --> 00:40:25.192
There is no contradiction because the two conventions answer different

00:40:25.192 --> 00:40:26.112
accounting questions.

00:40:26.112 --> 00:40:30.812
Neither pair of integer labels by itself specifies an experimentally measured

00:40:30.812 --> 00:40:32.372
full atomic charge distribution.

00:40:33.352 --> 00:40:37.932
Do not infer that carbon monoxide consists of a free carbon anion and oxygen

00:40:37.932 --> 00:40:41.132
cation, or that formal charge alone measures a bond dipole.

00:40:42.232 --> 00:40:45.841
State the convention before comparing charge labels across molecules,

00:40:45.841 --> 00:40:46.312
resonance

00:40:46.312 --> 00:40:48.432
contributors or coordination compounds.

00:40:48.672 --> 00:40:53.172
The molecular orbital model can distinguish an oxygen molecule from superoxide

00:40:53.172 --> 00:40:56.252
and peroxide without changing the two oxygen nuclei.

00:40:57.052 --> 00:41:00.912
In the usual introductory oxygen ordering, the neutral molecule has twelve

00:41:00.912 --> 00:41:05.172
valence electrons and two singly occupied degenerate pi antibonding orbitals.

00:41:05.912 --> 00:41:08.792
It has bond order two and two unpaired electrons.

00:41:09.772 --> 00:41:13.812
Add one electron to make superoxide: an antibonding orbital gains a partner,

00:41:14.452 --> 00:41:18.112
leaving one unpaired electron and lowering bond order to one point five.

00:41:18.912 --> 00:41:23.352
Add another to make peroxide: both pi antibonding orbitals are paired, bond

00:41:23.352 --> 00:41:26.952
order falls to one, and no unpaired electron remains in this simple

00:41:26.952 --> 00:41:27.512
configuration.

00:41:28.492 --> 00:41:32.792
The added electrons change populations rather than creating an extra oxygen

00:41:32.792 --> 00:41:34.952
atom or changing either nuclear charge.

00:41:35.672 --> 00:41:39.392
Within this related series, the decreasing bond order supports a qualitative

00:41:39.392 --> 00:41:42.552
trend toward a longer, weaker oxygen oxygen link.

00:41:42.552 --> 00:41:47.672
It is not a universal numerical bond length formula for every compound or an

00:41:47.672 --> 00:41:51.192
assertion that isolated ions and all solid salts have identical spectra.

00:41:52.172 --> 00:41:56.312
A Lewis peroxide single bond is compatible with this count, while oxygen's

00:41:56.312 --> 00:42:00.232
unpaired electrons require the molecular orbital occupation picture to explain

00:42:00.232 --> 00:42:01.812
its elementary paramagnetism.
